pi.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T14:30:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T14:35:50Z","body":"According to my (limited) testing, this seems to be working fine.\r\n\r\n* I hard coded the version check to below 4 on my build, as my Emscripten was higher, and I wanted to force the new code on.\r\n* I added debugging code within `get_entropy()` within the ifdefs to create a blank array, fill it with random data then fill it out, twice.\r\n* I printed before and after and confirmed it was zeroed before, and filled with random data after, and different random data on each run.\r\n\r\n```\r\n#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN_major__) && (__EMSCRIPTEN_major__ < 4 || (__EMSCRIPTEN_major__ == 2 && __EMSCRIPTEN_minor__ == 0 && __EMSCRIPTEN_tiny__ < 5))\r\n\t\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(godot_js_os_internal_getentropy(r_buffer + ofs, chunk), FAILED);\r\n\r\n\t\t// Test it is working\r\n\t\tfor (uint32_t t=0; t<2; t++)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tconst int test_length = 32;\r\n\t\t\tprint_line(\"testing entropy\");\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t// zero\r\n\t\t\tuint8_t data[test_length] = {};\r\n\r\n\t\t\t// print before filling with random\r\n\t\t\tfor (uint32_t n=0; n<test_length; n++)\r\n\t\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\tprint_line(\"\\t\" + itos(data[n]));\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\tgodot_js_os_internal_getentropy(data, test_length);\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t// print after filling with random\r\n\t\t\tfor (uint32_t n=0; n<test_length; n++)\r\n\t\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\tprint_line(\"\\t\" + itos(data[n]));\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n#else\r\n\t\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(getentropy(r_buffer + ofs, chunk), FAILED);\r\n#endif\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5357311940/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5371647592","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122647#issuecomment-5371647592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122647","id":5371647592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQCzWaA","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T15:06:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T15:06:06Z","body":"Sorry I'm traveling so I'll be brief.\r\n\r\nSee the attached changeset tested with emcc 1.39.9: [patch.diff.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31310691/patch.diff.txt)\r\n","author_